WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Welcome to our 2026 National Summit
on Artificial Intelligence.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.800
Welcome to our national audience
of higher educators.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.500
In this session, our panel—Jean Velonis,

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.400
Dr. Kathleen J. Kennedy,
and Elizabeth Hannan—

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.300
explores the critical intersection of human
agency and machine-led decision-making.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.300
As AI increasingly influences

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.600
education and career pathways,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.000
we must ask: can we truly understand,
challenge, or correct them?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.200
Today, we will break down this challenge
into five essential steps.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:39.000
I'm joined by an expert panel:
Jean Velonis from Salesforce,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.500
Dr. Kathleen J. Kennedy
from the University of Arizona,

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.800
and I'm Elizabeth Hannan from EarnLane.
Together, we bring three unique perspectives

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.800
on governing AI.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.000
We begin by identifying where the human
gets lost in automated systems

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.500
and discussing the critical threshold
between helpful AI assistance and dangerous

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.600
dependency on machine-generated outcomes.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.000
Furthermore, we examine where to place
necessary human checkpoints

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:17.000
when AI recommends credentials and how
institutional leaders can establish

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.000
durable boundaries that remain effective
despite rapid technological evolution.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.500
In our closing round, we synthesize these
discussions into actionable advice for you,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:33.500
focusing on what steps you can take tomorrow
to maintain oversight of these systems.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.500
Here are four core takeaways for your campus.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.500
Adopt a tiered framework,
prioritize functional transparency,

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:49.800
demand accountability from vendors,
and prepare your workforce
to govern algorithms effectively.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:55.000
This three-layer framework organizes
AI impact across platform credentialing,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.300
education system decisions,
and classroom learning,

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:05.200
with a mandatory audit layer in every section
to allow for pausing, reviewing, and pivoting.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.500
To turn these insights into practice,
follow these five steps.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.000
Map the decision landscape,
assign clear reviewers,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.000
audit your checkpoints,
ask vendors hard questions about their data,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.289
and build critical skills
among your team.

00:02:16.289 --> 00:02:18.169
We encourage you to stay connected

00:02:18.169 --> 00:02:19.609
with our panel and explore the

00:02:19.609 --> 00:02:21.809
resources provided to continue your

00:02:21.809 --> 00:02:23.489
journey in responsible AI

00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:25.329
governance. Thank you for joining

00:02:25.329 --> 00:02:26.609
our conversation today.
